\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7.2}{\ignorespaces Penalty against exact contact on the model problem ($841\xspace $ unknowns). Left: the largest penetration falls like $1/k_p$ but never reaches zero; the exact solution has no penetration (drawn at the plotting floor). Right: the condition number of the penalty matrix grows in proportion to $k_p$; the exact route solves a system whose condition number does not depend on any parameter.\relax }}{45}{figure.caption.88}%
